  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-25: "Yes let me know when done and continue with next tasks". Issue #3091 (read it in full: gh issue view 3091) and DI-172 in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md. Entry points on origin/master 2ac250cae4 (search by name): `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReevaluationJob.cs` `RedactPoliciesNotInForceAsync` (~1356) calls `SweepStoredEvidenceAsync` (~1384) with every Off/Retired ontology policy; it reads each policy's Signals by dedupe-key prefix in every status via `ReadPolicySignalsAsync(..., forRedactionSweep: true)`. The deleted-policy sweep (~556) shares `SweepStoredEvidenceAsync`. Task 209 (PR #3087, e9393ace47) solved the same shape for the close with one paged query joined to the not-in-force policies: read its POML (tasks/209-*.poml) and notes/task-209-notes.md first, and task 145's redaction rule (tasks/145-*.poml, its notes).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF, Dataverse SDK QueryExpression / LinkEntity paging, the ontology nightly re-evaluation job.</role>
  <goal>The not-in-force redaction sweep's Dataverse reads scale with the Signals whose stored evidence still needs redaction, not with every Signal of every Off/Retired policy; which evidence is redacted, and how, is unchanged.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Hypothesis from the issue (check it): find a stored marker that tells redacted evidence from unredacted (task 145 writes a redacted form; if it is detectable in a query, filter on it), and read only unredacted Signals of not-in-force policies in one paged query joined to sprk_policy, as task 209 did. If redaction leaves nothing a query can filter on, STOP and report rather than adding a column. Keep the deleted-policy sweep unchanged unless a test proves both. Keep the one-failure-per-policy-per-run accounting, forRedactionSweep mode (unparseable keys skipped silently), the D-170 policy set, D-61 (never stamp an unchanged Signal), and task 204/209: a truncated read is reported and fails the run. Read `git log -5` on SignalReevaluationJob.cs; run /conflict-check (ebilling-r1 merges into Signals code).</background>
  </context>
